{number: 146}
{title: O the Help that God has Given}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O the [G] help that God has given
To His [C] children on the [G] way,
Leading from earth's shadowy paths
To [D7] everlasting [G] day!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] Trust Him, trust Him,
He will never [C] leave thee nor for-[G] sake;
Trust Him, trust Him,
[D7] Every promise [G] keep.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O the [G] love of God our Savior,
Reaching [C] downward to the [G] lost,
Lifting souls from sin and ruin,
[D7] Paid for at so great a [G] cost!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O the [G] grace that never faileth,
Flowing [C] freely from a-[G] bove,
Filling every hungry spirit
[D7] With the fullness of His [G] love!
{end_of_verse}
